<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>

		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
		<OutputType>Library</OutputType>
		<IsTrimmable>false</IsTrimmable>
		<Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
		
		<Description><![CDATA[
Nalix.Logging is a lightweight, asynchronous logging subsystem designed STRICTLY for DEVELOPMENT environments within the Nalix ecosystem.

⚠️ WARNING: This logging library is NOT intended for production use. It is designed to provide quick, debug-friendly console and file outputs during the development phase. For production environments, please use a robust, production-ready logging framework such as Serilog, NLog, or an OpenTelemetry-compatible sink.
		]]></Description>

		<PackageReleaseNotes><![CDATA[
- Development Only: Explicitly marked as a development-only tool. Do NOT use in production environments.
- Asynchronous Performance: Basic channel-based logging engine designed for non-blocking local execution.
- Simple Targets: Built-in sinks including basic file I/O and console output for debugging purposes.
- Unified Facade: Provides simple NLogix access points for development-phase logging.
		]]></PackageReleaseNotes>

		<AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>

	</PropertyGroup>

	<Import Project="..\Nalix.Build.props" />
	<Import Project="..\Package.Build.props" />

	<ItemGroup>
		<ProjectReference Include="..\Nalix.Framework\Nalix.Framework.csproj" />
		<ProjectReference Include="..\Nalix.Abstractions\Nalix.Abstractions.csproj" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.8" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
